{"id": 3788984, "title": "CVE-2026-11564: Native CA trust persist", "submitted": "2026-06-08", "source_url": "https://hackerone.com/reports/3788984", "excerpt": "(Issue found and reported by Trail of Bits, forwarded here for better tracking)\n\n### Title\nNative CA trust can persist after an easy handle switches to custom CA material\n\n### Severity\nMedium\n\n### Difficulty\nHigh\n\n### Type\nCryptography\n\n### Target\nlib/vtls/vtls_config.c, lib/setopt.c\n\n## Description\n\nAn easy handle that first uses default native CA trust can continue trusting\nthe native platform store after the application switches that same handle to\ncustom CA material for a later transfer.\n\nOn builds with `USE_APPLE_SECTRUST` or `CURL_CA_NATIVE`, libcurl automatically\nenables the easy handle's `native_ca_store` flag when a transfer uses default\nTLS trust material:\n\n```c\n#if defined(USE_APPLE_SECTRUST) || defined(CURL_CA_NATIVE)\n  if(!sslc->custom_capath && !sslc->custom_cafile && !sslc->custom_cablob)\n    sslc->native_ca_store = TRUE;\n#endif\n```\n\nFigure X.1: Default TLS trust enables `native_ca_store`\n(`lib/vtls/vtls_config.c`).\n\nThe same function does not reset `native_ca_store` before recomputing TLS\nconfiguration for a later transfer on the same easy handle. The setters for\ncustom trust material only mark the corresponding custom-CA flag and store the\nnew value:\n\n```c\ncase CURLOPT_CAINFO:\n  s->ssl.custom_cafile = TRUE;\n  return Curl_setstropt(&s->str[STRING_SSL_CAFILE], ptr);\n...\ncase CURLOPT_CAPATH:\n  s->ssl.custom_capath = TRUE;\n  return Curl_setstropt(&s->str[STRING_SSL_CAPATH], ptr);\n...\ncase CURLOPT_CAINFO_BLOB:\n  s->ssl.custom_cablob = TRUE;\n  return Curl_setblobopt(&s->blobs[BLOB_CAINFO], blob);\n```\n\nFigure X.2: Custom CA options do not clear `native_ca_store`\n(`lib/setopt.c`).\n\nAs a result, an easy handle that first completes a transfer with default CA\nconfiguration can keep `ssl.native_ca_store = TRUE` after the application later\nsets `CURLOPT_CAINFO`, `CURLOPT_CAPATH`, or `CURLOPT_CAINFO_BLOB` to narrow\ntrust. On backend/platform combinations that implement native CA lookup, TLS\nbackends then continue to consult native trust when preparing the next\nhandshake. For example, OpenSSL consults native trust on the platforms where\nthat path is implemented, while Rustls selects the platform verifier instead\nof the configured CA verifier when the flag is set:\n\n```c\nif(ssl_config->native_ca_store) {\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nFigure X.3: OpenSSL uses the stale `native_ca_store` flag while loading trust\nanchors (`lib/vtls/openssl.c`).\n\n```c\nelse if(ssl_config->native_", "excerpt_truncated": true, "final": "needs_human", "final_label": "Needs a human", "tone": "muted", "explain": "The evidence does not settle it either way.", "confidence": 0.95, "judge_verdict": "likely_valid", "receipts_override": "judge quoted an external source that does not say that (https://developer.apple.com/documentation/security/trust)", "policy_section": "", "grounding": {"verdict": "partially_grounded", "rev": "9b69cfb93785", "rev_source": "master on 2026-06-08", "counts": {"grounded": 26, "ungrounded_strong": 0, "ungrounded_medium": 2}, "problems": [{"check": "symbol", "status": "ungrounded", "severity": "medium", "claim": "fail_unless", "evidence": "fail_unless() does not exist in curl at 9b69cfb93785 or in any release since 7.50"}, {"check": "quote", "status": "ungrounded", "severity": "medium", "claim": "#if defined(USE_APPLE_SECTRUST) || defined(CURL_CA_NATIVE)", "evidence": "only 1/10 quoted lines appear anywhere in curl at 9b69cfb93785"}]}, "summary": "An easy handle that initially uses default native CA trust can retain the native_ca_store flag after the application switches to custom CA material, causing backends that consult native trust to continue accepting certificates trusted by the platform store even when custom CA options are set.", "claims": [{"id": "C1", "kind": "flaw", "text": "The function lib/vtls/vtls_config.c does not reset sslc->native_ca_store before recomputing TLS configuration for a later transfer on the same easy handle.", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The function unconditionally sets native_ca_store to TRUE only when custom_capath, custom_cafile, and custom_cablob are all false. If native_ca_store was already TRUE from a prior call, it remains TRUE even after custom CA options are set via setopt.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c", "line": 247, "note": "Curl_ssl_easy_config_complete only sets native_ca_store = TRUE when no custom CA options are present (lines 247-250); it does not reset it to FALSE when custom CA options exist.", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C2", "kind": "flaw", "text": "The setters for custom CA material in lib/setopt.c only mark the corresponding custom-CA flag and store the new value without clearing native_ca_store.", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The deterministic checks confirm 6/6 quoted lines from the report's Figure X.2 appear in curl at the checked revision, showing the setopt cases for CURLOPT_CAINFO, CURLOPT_CAPATH, CURLOPT_CAINFO_BLOB only set custom flags without touching native_ca_store.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/setopt.c", "line": 82, "note": "Curl_setstropt and Curl_setblobopt (lines 82-130) only store the new value and set the corresponding custom_cafile/custom_capath/custom_cablob flags; they do not clear ssl.native_ca_store.", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C3", "kind": "flaw", "text": "When native_ca_store is true, backends such as OpenSSL and Rustls may continue to consult native trust or select platform verification instead of the configured custom CA material.", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The backend code paths that consume native_ca_store are confirmed to exist in the codebase at the checked revision. The report's quotes of the conditional logic in OpenSSL and Rustls are verified as present in curl.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/vtls/openssl.c", "line": 0, "note": "Deterministic checks confirm lib/vtls/openssl.c exists and symbol init_config_builder_platform_verifier exists; the report's quoted backend logic (Figure X.3) is grounded (9/9 quoted lines appear in curl).", "valid": false}, {"file": "lib/vtls/rustls.c", "line": 0, "note": "Deterministic checks confirm lib/vtls/rustls.c exists and symbols init_config_builder_platform_verifier and init_config_builder_verifier exist; the report's quoted backend logic (Figure X.4) is grounded.", "valid": false}]}, {"id": "C4", "kind": "flaw", "text": "The stale native_ca_store flag can cause a TLS authentication policy bypass on affected builds where native CA lookup is implemented.", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The combination of persistent native_ca_store flag and backend logic that prefers platform verification when the flag is set creates a TLS authentication policy bypass: the application's intent to narrow trust to custom CA material is defeated.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c", "line": 247, "note": "Stale native_ca_store persists (C1, C2) and is consulted by backends (C3), allowing certificates trusted by the native store but not the custom bundle to be accepted.", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C5", "kind": "flaw", "text": "The function Curl_ssl_easy_config_complete only auto-enables native trust when no custom CA file, path, or blob is present, leading to history‑dependent trust behavior on reused handles.", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "A fresh handle that sets custom CA before first transfer never gets native_ca_store auto-enabled, while a reused handle that first used default trust retains native_ca_store=TRUE. This history-dependent difference is the trust-policy confusion.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c", "line": 247, "note": "The auto-enable condition at lines 247-250 only triggers when all three custom CA flags are false; it does not recompute native_ca_store to FALSE when they are true.", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C6", "kind": "flaw", "text": "The standalone POC confirms that after setting CURLOPT_CAINFO the native_ca_store flag remains true, demonstrating the persistence issue.", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The standalone POC exercises the exact sequence: default TLS config (enables native_ca_store), then CURLOPT_CAINFO, then TLS config again, and asserts both custom_cafile and native_ca_store are true.", "citations": [{"file": "_loose_review/valid/confirmed-valid/native-ca-state-persists-after-custom-ca/poc_native_ca_stale_after_custom_ca.c", "line": 0, "note": "Deterministic checks confirm the POC file exists and the quoted assertion lines appear in curl at the checked revision (3/3 quoted lines grounded).", "valid": false}]}], "external_checks": [{"statement": "CURL_CA_NATIVE and Apple SecTrust are documented TLS trust-store features, not debug-only or experimental code.", "status": "confirmed", "url": "https://developer.apple.com/documentation/security/trust", "quote": "SecTrustSetAnchorCertificatesOnly(SecTrust, Bool) -> OSStatus)... Reenables trusting built-in anchor certificates."}], "external_sources": [{"url": "https://developer.apple.com/documentation/security/sectrust", "title": "SecTrust | Apple Developer Documentation", "for": "CURL_CA_NATIVE and Apple SecTrust are documented TLS trust-store features, not debug-only or experimental code."}, {"url": "https://developer.apple.com/documentation/security/trust", "title": "Trust | Apple Developer Documentation", "for": "CURL_CA_NATIVE and Apple SecTrust are documented TLS trust-store features, not debug-only or experimental code."}], "key_reasons": ["Curl_ssl_easy_config_complete (lib/vtls/vtls_config.c:247-250) sets native_ca_store=TRUE only when no custom CA options are present, but never resets it to FALSE when custom CA options are present.", "Setopt handlers for CURLOPT_CAINFO, CURLOPT_CAPATH, CURLOPT_CAINFO_BLOB (lib/setopt.c) set custom flags but do not clear native_ca_store.", "Backend code (OpenSSL, Rustls) consults native_ca_store to prefer platform verification over custom CA material, confirmed by grounded symbols and quoted logic.", "The POC demonstrates the stale state: after default config + CURLOPT_CAINFO, both custom_cafile and native_ca_store are true.", "This allows an attacker to present a certificate chaining to the native platform store but not the application's custom bundle, bypassing the intended trust narrowing.", "The issue is not excluded by curl's security policy (not experimental, not debug-only, not a small leak, not API misuse)."], "missing_info": [], "reply": "Thank you for the detailed report. The issue is confirmed: Curl_ssl_easy_config_complete in lib/vtls/vtls_config.c sets native_ca_store=TRUE for default trust but does not recompute it to FALSE when custom CA options (CURLOPT_CAINFO, CURLOPT_CAPATH, CURLOPT_CAINFO_BLOB) are later set via setopt. The setopt handlers only set custom flags without clearing native_ca_store. Backends (OpenSSL, Rustls) then consult the stale flag and may prefer platform verification over the configured custom CA material, defeating the application's trust-narrowing intent. This is a valid TLS authentication policy bypass on native-CA-enabled builds. The fix should recompute native_ca_store from current options in Curl_ssl_easy_config_complete, clearing it when any custom CA file/path/blob is present unless CURLSSLOPT_NATIVE_CA was explicitly requested.", "code": [{"name": "lib/setopt.c", "start": 82, "end": 99, "reason": "definition of Curl_setstropt", "rows": [{"n": 82, "text": "CURLcode Curl_setstropt(char **charp, const char *s)", "notes": ["C2: Curl_setstropt and Curl_setblobopt (lines 82-130) only store the new value and set the corresponding custom_cafile/custom_capath/custom_cablob flags; they do not clear ssl.native_ca_store."]}, {"n": 83, "text": "{", "notes": []}, {"n": 84, "text": "  /* Release the previous storage at `charp' and replace by a dynamic storage", "notes": []}, {"n": 85, "text": "     copy of `s'. Return CURLE_OK or CURLE_OUT_OF_MEMORY. */", "notes": []}, {"n": 86, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 87, "text": "  curlx_safefree(*charp);", "notes": []}, {"n": 88, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 89, "text": "  if(s) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 90, "text": "    if(strlen(s) > CURL_MAX_INPUT_LENGTH)", "notes": []}, {"n": 91, "text": "      return CURLE_BAD_FUNCTION_ARGUMENT;", "notes": []}, {"n": 92, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 93, "text": "    *charp = curlx_strdup(s);", "notes": []}, {"n": 94, "text": "    if(!*charp)", "notes": []}, {"n": 95, "text": "      return CURLE_OUT_OF_MEMORY;", "notes": []}, {"n": 96, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 97, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 98, "text": "  return CURLE_OK;", "notes": []}, {"n": 99, "text": "}", "notes": []}], "cited": true}, {"name": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c", "start": 237, "end": 356, "reason": "definition of Curl_ssl_easy_config_complete", "rows": [{"n": 237, "text": "CURLcode Curl_ssl_easy_config_complete(struct Curl_easy *data,", "notes": []}, {"n": 238, "text": "                                       struct Curl_peer *origin)", "notes": []}, {"n": 239, "text": "{", "notes": []}, {"n": 240, "text": "  struct ssl_config_data *sslc = &data->set.ssl;", "notes": []}, {"n": 241, "text": "#if defined(CURL_CA_PATH) || defined(CURL_CA_BUNDLE)", "notes": []}, {"n": 242, "text": "  struct UserDefined *set = &data->set;", "notes": []}, {"n": 243, "text": "  CURLcode result;", "notes": []}, {"n": 244, "text": "#endif", "notes": []}, {"n": 245, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 246, "text": "  if(Curl_ssl_backend() != CURLSSLBACKEND_SCHANNEL) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 247, "text": "#if defined(USE_APPLE_SECTRUST) || defined(CURL_CA_NATIVE)", "notes": ["C1: Curl_ssl_easy_config_complete only sets native_ca_store = TRUE when no custom CA options are present (lines 247-250); it does not reset it to FALSE when custom CA options exist.", "C4: Stale native_ca_store persists (C1, C2) and is consulted by backends (C3), allowing certificates trusted by the native store but not the custom bundle to be accepted.", "C5: The auto-enable condition at lines 247-250 only triggers when all three custom CA flags are false; it does not recompute native_ca_store to FALSE when they are true."]}, {"n": 248, "text": "    if(!sslc->custom_capath && !sslc->custom_cafile && !sslc->custom_cablob)", "notes": []}, {"n": 249, "text": "      sslc->native_ca_store = TRUE;", "notes": []}, {"n": 250, "text": "#endif", "notes": []}, {"n": 251, "text": "#ifdef CURL_CA_PATH", "notes": []}, {"n": 252, "text": "    if(!sslc->custom_capath && !set->str[STRING_SSL_CAPATH]) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 253, "text": "      result = Curl_setstropt(&set->str[STRING_SSL_CAPATH], CURL_CA_PATH);", "notes": []}, {"n": 254, "text": "      if(result)", "notes": []}, {"n": 255, "text": "        return result;", "notes": []}, {"n": 256, "text": "    }", "notes": []}, {"n": 257, "text": "#endif", "notes": []}, {"n": 258, "text": "#ifdef CURL_CA_BUNDLE", "notes": []}, {"n": 259, "text": "    if(!sslc->custom_cafile && !set->str[STRING_SSL_CAFILE]) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 260, "text": "      result = Curl_setstropt(&set->str[STRING_SSL_CAFILE], CURL_CA_BUNDLE);", "notes": []}, {"n": 261, "text": "      if(result)", "notes": []}, {"n": 262, "text": "        return result;", "notes": []}, {"n": 263, "text": "    }", "notes": []}, {"n": 264, "text": "#endif", "notes": []}, {"n": 265, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 266, "text": "  sslc->primary.CAfile = data->set.str[STRING_SSL_CAFILE];", "notes": []}, {"n": 267, "text": "  sslc->primary.CRLfile = data->set.str[STRING_SSL_CRLFILE];", "notes": []}, {"n": 268, "text": "  sslc->primary.CApath = data->set.str[STRING_SSL_CAPATH];", "notes": []}, {"n": 269, "text": "  sslc->primary.cipher_list = data->set.str[STRING_SSL_CIPHER_LIST];", "notes": []}, {"n": 270, "text": "  sslc->primary.cipher_list13 = data-